---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout>
	<main class="type-specimen" aria-label="Type specimen">
		<section class="col">
			<div class="col-header">
				<span class="col-header-label">Light surface · #f7f6f1</span>
				<div class="swatches">
					<div
						class="swatch"
						style="background:#111317"
						title="#111317 primary"
					></div>
					<div
						class="swatch"
						style="background:#f7f6f1;border-color:rgba(0,0,0,.18)"
						title="#f7f6f1 secondary"
					></div>
					<div
						class="swatch"
						style="background:#5a5d65"
						title="#5a5d65 muted"
					></div>
					<div
						class="swatch"
						style="background:#9498a2"
						title="#9498a2 faint"
					></div>
					<div
						class="swatch"
						style="background:#8badb8"
						title="#8badb8 darkaccent"
					></div>
					<div
						class="swatch"
						style="background:#1c2e33"
						title="#1c2e33 darkhighlight"
					></div>
					<div
						class="swatch"
						style="background:#5f1b36"
						title="#5f1b36 lightaccent"
					></div>
					<div
						class="swatch"
						style="background:#f0e0e6;border-color:rgba(0,0,0,.12)"
						title="#f0e0e6 lighthighlight"
					></div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="block">
				<span class="meta">h1 · Syne 800</span>
				<p class="t-h1">Dekamus<br><span class="a-light">association</span></p>
				<div class="spec">
					<span class="spec-item"><span>size</span>clamp(56–80px)</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>leading</span>1.00</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>tracking</span>−0.03em</span>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="block">
				<span class="meta">h2 · Syne 700</span>
				<p class="t-h2">The weight of<br>written thought</p>
				<div class="spec">
					<span class="spec-item"><span>size</span>clamp(38–51px)</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>leading</span>1.08</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>tracking</span>−0.02em</span>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="block">
				<span class="meta">h3 · Source Serif 4 600</span>
				<p class="t-h3">A sentence holds<br>its own gravity</p>
				<div class="spec">
					<span class="spec-item"><span>size</span>clamp(27–35px)</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>leading</span>1.20</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>tracking</span>−0.01em</span>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="block">
				<span class="meta">h4 · Source Serif 4 600</span>
				<p class="t-h4">Contrast builds clarity between structure and flow</p>
				<div class="spec">
					<span class="spec-item"><span>size</span>clamp(19–24px)</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>leading</span>1.30</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>tracking</span>0em</span>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="block">
				<span class="meta">body lead · Source Serif 4 400</span>
				<p class="t-lead">
					Reading is a performance of the eye across space. The rhythm of a
					paragraph lives in its leading—too tight and the eye loses its path;
					too loose and the reader floats untethered between lines.
				</p>
				<div class="spec">
					<span class="spec-item"><span>size</span>clamp(17–19px)</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>leading</span>1.75</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>tracking</span>0.01em</span>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="block">
				<span class="meta">body · Source Serif 4 400</span>
				<p class="t-body">
					The paragraph is the unit of thought. Each line break is a breath,
					each sentence a step. Good spacing lets the meaning settle before the
					next idea arrives, quietly, without interruption. Typography is
					invisible architecture—most felt when it fails.
				</p>
				<div class="spec">
					<span class="spec-item"><span>size</span>clamp(16–17px)</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>leading</span>1.70</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>tracking</span>0.005em</span>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="block">
				<span class="meta">small · Source Serif 4 400</span>
				<p class="t-small" style="color:var(--muted)">
					Footnotes carry the weight of evidence. At smaller sizes, leading must
					increase proportionally—the eye needs more air between lines to follow
					text without effort or fatigue.
				</p>
				<div class="spec">
					<span class="spec-item"><span>size</span>13.4px</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>leading</span>1.65</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>tracking</span>0.01em</span>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="block">
				<span class="meta">caption · Source Serif 4 300 Italic</span>
				<p class="t-caption" style="color:var(--muted)">
					Fig. 1 — Visual hierarchy emerges from contrast in weight, size, and
					spatial rhythm rather than from decoration alone. The page breathes
					when type is trusted to do the work.
				</p>
				<div class="spec">
					<span class="spec-item"><span>size</span>12.3px</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>leading</span>1.60</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>tracking</span>0.02em</span>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="block">
				<span class="meta">mono · Victor Mono Italic 400</span>
				<p class="t-mono" style="color:var(--lightaccent)">
					const rhythm = lineHeight * fontSize;<br>// spacing makes prose
					readable
				</p>
				<div class="spec">
					<span class="spec-item"><span>size</span>14px</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>leading</span>1.60</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>tracking</span>0.03em</span>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="block">
				<span class="meta">mono sm · Victor Mono Italic 400</span>
				<p class="t-mono-sm" style="color:var(--faint)">
					font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.55; letter-spacing: 0.04em;
				</p>
				<div class="spec">
					<span class="spec-item"><span>size</span>12.3px</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>leading</span>1.55</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>tracking</span>0.04em</span>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<div class="rule"></div>

		<section class="col col--dark">
			<div class="col-header">
				<span class="col-header-label">Dark surface · #111317</span>
				<div class="swatches">
					<div
						class="swatch"
						style="background:#f7f6f1;border-color:rgba(255,255,255,.08)"
						title="#f7f6f1"
					></div>
					<div
						class="swatch"
						style="background:#111317;border-color:rgba(255,255,255,.12)"
						title="#111317"
					></div>
					<div class="swatch" style="background:#5a5d65" title="#5a5d65"></div>
					<div class="swatch" style="background:#9498a2" title="#9498a2"></div>
					<div class="swatch" style="background:#8badb8" title="#8badb8"></div>
					<div class="swatch" style="background:#1c2e33" title="#1c2e33"></div>
					<div class="swatch" style="background:#5f1b36" title="#5f1b36"></div>
					<div
						class="swatch"
						style="background:#f0e0e6;border-color:rgba(0,0,0,.15)"
						title="#f0e0e6"
					></div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="block">
				<span class="meta">h1 · Syne 800</span>
				<p class="t-h1">
					Association<br><span style="color:#8badb8">Dekamus</span>
				</p>
				<div class="spec">
					<span class="spec-item"><span>size</span>clamp(56–80px)</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>leading</span>1.00</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>tracking</span>−0.03em</span>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="block">
				<span class="meta">h2 · Syne 700</span>
				<p class="t-h2">The weight of<br>written thought</p>
				<div class="spec">
					<span class="spec-item"><span>size</span>clamp(38–51px)</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>leading</span>1.08</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>tracking</span>−0.02em</span>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="block">
				<span class="meta">h3 · Source Serif 4 600</span>
				<p class="t-h3">A sentence holds<br>its own gravity</p>
				<div class="spec">
					<span class="spec-item"><span>size</span>clamp(27–35px)</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>leading</span>1.20</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>tracking</span>−0.01em</span>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="block">
				<span class="meta">h4 · Source Serif 4 600</span>
				<p class="t-h4">Contrast builds clarity between structure and flow</p>
				<div class="spec">
					<span class="spec-item"><span>size</span>clamp(19–24px)</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>leading</span>1.30</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>tracking</span>0em</span>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="block">
				<span class="meta">body lead · Source Serif 4 400</span>
				<p class="t-lead">
					Reading is a performance of the eye across space. The rhythm of a
					paragraph lives in its leading—too tight and the eye loses its path;
					too loose and the reader floats untethered between lines.
				</p>
				<div class="spec">
					<span class="spec-item"><span>size</span>clamp(17–19px)</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>leading</span>1.75</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>tracking</span>0.01em</span>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="block">
				<span class="meta">body · Source Serif 4 400</span>
				<p class="t-body">
					The paragraph is the unit of thought. Each line break is a breath,
					each sentence a step. Good spacing lets the meaning settle before the
					next idea arrives, quietly, without interruption. Typography is
					invisible architecture—most felt when it fails.
				</p>
				<div class="spec">
					<span class="spec-item"><span>size</span>clamp(16–17px)</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>leading</span>1.70</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>tracking</span>0.005em</span>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="block">
				<span class="meta">small · Source Serif 4 400</span>
				<p class="t-small" style="color:#9498a2">
					Footnotes carry the weight of evidence. At smaller sizes, leading must
					increase proportionally—the eye needs more air between lines to follow
					text without effort or fatigue.
				</p>
				<div class="spec">
					<span class="spec-item"><span>size</span>13.4px</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>leading</span>1.65</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>tracking</span>0.01em</span>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="block">
				<span class="meta">caption · Source Serif 4 300 Italic</span>
				<p class="t-caption" style="color:#9498a2">
					Fig. 1 — Visual hierarchy emerges from contrast in weight, size, and
					spatial rhythm rather than from decoration alone. The page breathes
					when type is trusted to do the work.
				</p>
				<div class="spec">
					<span class="spec-item"><span>size</span>12.3px</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>leading</span>1.60</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>tracking</span>0.02em</span>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="block">
				<span class="meta">mono · Victor Mono Italic 400</span>
				<p class="t-mono" style="color:#8badb8">
					const rhythm = lineHeight * fontSize;<br>// spacing makes prose
					readable
				</p>
				<div class="spec">
					<span class="spec-item"><span>size</span>14px</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>leading</span>1.60</span>
					<span class="spec-item"><span>tracking</span>0.03em</span>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="block">
				<span class="meta">mono sm · Victor Mono Italic 400</span>
				<p class="t-mono-sm" style="color:#5a5d65">
